WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:03.959
Let's go to our next caller from the two six
two area code.

00:00:03.959 --> 00:00:05.780
Who's calling today from two six two

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:07.220
Oh, hi David.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.160
Can you hear me?

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.640
Yes I can.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:16.090
Hey, I'm one of your right wind sands and
I'm wondering if you have any idea of when

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:21.350
all of this a low hanging fruit that our generation
is into when we'll finally pick that rank

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:25.939
choice vote cut the military in half term
limits.

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:27.160
This sort of thing.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.029
I don't have an answer unfortunately.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:34.340
I mean, I, I would, I would like to see, uh,
many of those, uh, ideas implemented soon.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:39.280
Uh, I agree that they are low hanging fruit
in the sense that these are pretty obvious

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.040
things that we should be doing.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.620
It's not low hanging fruit in the sense that
it's easy to accomplish politically.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:45.620
There would be big opposition.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.390
So I don't know in what sense if you mean
low hanging fruit as like, Hey, we should

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.490
obviously do these things.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:51.490
I'm with you.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:54.379
If you mean low hanging fruit in it should
have been easy to do them already.

00:00:54.379 --> 00:00:55.760
I don't know about that.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:01.090
Well, I mean, uh, you know, I have plenty
of left wing and right wind fans and they

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.939
are not fans friends and they all seem to
agree on, on this list.

00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:07.530
But um, yeah, why hasn't it happened?

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:13.119
Well, a lot of those things challenge the
institutions of power.

00:01:13.119 --> 00:01:14.950
So term limits.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:18.719
Everybody who got in got in without term limits.

00:01:18.719 --> 00:01:23.499
They're not particularly incentivized to put
in place term limits that might get them out

00:01:23.499 --> 00:01:24.909
of office.

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:30.820
A lot of the people that got in got in supporting
the military industrial complex being funded

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.929
by defense contractors, et cetera.

00:01:32.929 --> 00:01:36.779
So they're not really the people who are going
to go in and cut the size of the military

00:01:36.779 --> 00:01:37.779
in half.

00:01:37.779 --> 00:01:42.279
So you have to understand that, that there's
a, there's unaligned incentives there.

00:01:42.279 --> 00:01:45.469
Well, hopefully if we can change those incentives.

00:01:45.469 --> 00:01:47.689
Can I ask one other quick question?

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:48.729
Yeah.

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:54.469
Um, so I have some money left for me in a
Vanguard healthcare account and I'm wondering

00:01:54.469 --> 00:01:58.880
what will happen to that sort of account,
uh, is some sort of Medicare for all those

00:01:58.880 --> 00:01:59.880
tests.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:06.450
Um, my sense is that any accounts that are
for sort of like predesignated healthcare

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.289
spending, so I think this would include like
HSHS and so on and so forth.

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:16.760
I assume that if Medicare for all, uh, takes
place, all of that money will be a sort of

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:21.790
allowed to be moved out of those sequestered
funds that have to be used for health care.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:23.310
It's a healthcare mutual fund.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.019
It's a healthcare mutual fund.

00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:26.019
So,

00:02:26.019 --> 00:02:27.489
Oh, we just invest in healthcare companies.

00:02:27.489 --> 00:02:28.489
Yeah.

00:02:28.489 --> 00:02:30.980
You're going to want to get out of that.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.739
I think if Medicare for all passes.

00:02:32.739 --> 00:02:34.989
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:34.989 --> 00:02:35.989
Right.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:36.989
Good to know.

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:37.989
All right.

00:02:37.989 --> 00:02:38.989
Very good.

00:02:38.989 --> 00:02:39.989
Thank you so much for the call.

00:02:39.989 --> 00:02:40.989
I appreciate it.

00:02:40.989 --> 00:02:41.989
Let's take a quick break.

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:44.459
If you're holding, uh, don't hang up because
we'll go right back to the phones right after

00:02:44.459 --> 00:02:45.159
the short break

